    "result": "Perfect! The bug is fixed. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe issue was that the `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't passing the `--ci` flag to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI. The main program's `.option('--ci', ...)` was consuming the flag before it reached the `gate` subcommand.\n\n## Solution\n\nI made two changes to `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:\n\n1. **Line 604**: Added `.enablePositionalOptions()` to the main program to allow subcommands to receive options\n2. **Line 740**: Added `.passThroughOptions()` to the `gate` command to prevent the parent from parsing options and ensure they're passed through as arguments\n\nWith these changes, when `frai gate init --ci` is run, the `--ci` flag is now correctly passed to the frai-gate CLI, which creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` as expected.\n\nThe fix has been tested and confirmed working\u2014the workflow file is now created correctly when using `frai gate init --ci`.",
